per bowl they were  like are you available for super bowl  tomorrow and i was like yeah they're  like okay it's for drake i was like  okay cool yeah i'm available were you  sitting very casually i couldn't believe  it as soon as i held that phone i was  hopping up and down i could not but it  happened so fast i mean from that phone  call i probably didn't sleep for the  next 48 hours for someone living in a  studio apartment with only a small  kitchenette at the time catering a large  party at the home of a superstar was a  game changer for the rookie chef towards  the end when it kind of started dying  down he came in the kitchen and we just  started talking i'm like i'm eager i'm  young i'm hungry i'm just like do you  have a chef  you know i'm just like griers saw an  opening and ran with it she worked with  drake for years and even went on tour  with him but you know what my favorite  part of that story that happened because  you asked them do you have a private  chef  so many people don't take that step  that's such an important lesson you  never know i mean when an opportunity is  there you have to take it you know and  you have to realize that you may not get  this chance again you have to make sure  that you go above and beyond because it  can either be the gateway to your next  one or it could be your last  you know i don't know if it's the  truffle honey but i just got chills  rare ingredients and raw talent drove  the la native from the start when did  you decide that you wanted to be a chef  i had a lot of different jobs in high  school just stayed busy i just felt like  you know what i could become a private  chef i was naturally great at cooking  i'm really tall so i started cooking  younger probably even a lot of people as  soon as you could reach as soon as i  could reach the stove i was like  scrambling eggs for chef kk nothing  seems out of reach these days i only  had a plan to become a private chef and  that has taken me further than i ever  would have imagined with her growing  roster of clients and her duties as the  executive chef at west hollywood's 40  love sports bar grier's plate is full  what was drake's favorite any of these  guys  definitely had the buffalo chicken on  there i mean that's a staple leave no  chip behind  none it's been a quite a journey  and a reminder that hard work sprinkled  with a little luck can be a powerful  recipe for success  for cbs mornings i'm lilia luciano in  los angeles  [Music]  nachos anyone ah really good i will  point out and i applaud this that the  guacamole clearly had no tomatoes in it  i'm a no tomato guacamole guy yeah it's  again a thicker guacamole um also  interesting that lily is there she's  working right that's an interview she's  on the job but she was eating that you  have to yeah you have to how do you not  and i do love what she said there though  that it's the opportunity when you have  that opportunity you never know is it  your next opportunity or is that your  last
 

